A||N||12||pherder||How to have your Fiero do 160 MPH!||||10||
Z||000000||pherder||02-06-2000||04:01 PM||||I will let you people in on a little "secret"!<P>When I had my Ferrari 308 kit car with the EuroDash interior, it came with a 120 MPH speedo.  Whenever I showed it, kids would look into the interior and state something like "... It will only go 120 MPH!!)<P>I got tired of that even though it had a stock 87 Fiero GT drivetrain and probably could only do 120+ ... but that is another thread ...  So I changed out the 120 MPH speedo for a 160 VDO Speedo.  <P>I would then get the "Wow, it will do 160 MPH!" statements.  Next question that would come out of most mouths was "How fast will it go?"  I got tired of telling them that it would do the speed limit so I would tell them I have seen the speedo at 160 MPH while in the car!!! and they would be VERY impressed!!  Doesn't take much...<P>What I didn't tell them and this is the "secret" is the 160 VDO Speedo self tests itself when powered up by going from 0 to 160 and then back to 0 and then it would register the speed.<P>I could look into their faces and without lying, tell them I have seen the speedo pegged out!  And you can too!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||10
Z||000001||Patrick||02-06-2000||04:14 PM||||<BR>Whenever kids get close enough to read my speedo, I tell them to stay away from the car! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||Phil||02-06-2000||07:26 PM||||I have the same speedo in my Lambo. If you really want to fake them out set the calibration to about 3000 pulses per mile. Then when you go 75mph it will read 100||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||02-06-2000||07:44 PM||||Phil, <P>I would never get rides ...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>BTW, the fastest the car ever went was 95 MPH.  That was with the wife driving trying to pass a large RV on a two lane road that had too many curves and not enough room to pass.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Less than a mile after we passed the RV, the road became 4 lanes.<P>Paul||||reg||12
